<section class="process_section"><div class="section-inner process_layout"><div class="networks_header"><h2 class="process_h2">How an engagement runs</h2></div><div class="work_tabs w-tabs" data-current="Tab 1" data-duration-in="300" data-duration-out="100" data-easing="ease"><div aria-label="Engagement type" class="process_tabs w-tab-menu"><a class="process_tab w-inline-block w-tab-link w--current" data-w-tab="Tab 1">Financial institutions</a><a class="process_tab w-inline-block w-tab-link" data-w-tab="Tab 2">Protocols and products</a><a class="process_tab w-inline-block w-tab-link" data-w-tab="Tab 3">Ecosystems and foundations</a></div><div class="work_panels w-tab-content"><div class="w-tab-pane w--tab-active" data-w-tab="Tab 1"><ul aria-label="Financial institutions" class="process_steps" role="list"><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">1</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Scoping</h3><p class="process_step-body">One technical session with your lead: who holds admin, mint and burn authority; custody and key management; freeze, clawback, allow and deny lists; KYT; the bridge to your core banking.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> the end-to-end process, who does what.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">2</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Structure</h3><p class="process_step-body">NDA, then an MOU with the scope cut into milestones your team can verify. Where an ecosystem program applies, we scope and draft the application; where it doesn't, we say so.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> signed MOU, milestone plan, funding application where one applies.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">3</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Build</h3><p class="process_step-body">A first release scoped to two or three use cases and designed to scale, on testnet with your operations team, each milestone validated with you and, where relevant, the network's foundation.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> contracts and integration live on testnet, validated milestone by milestone.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">4</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Mainnet and after</h3><p class="process_step-body">Deployment, runbooks and handover, then the changes production surfaces. We stay on the account.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> mainnet deployment, runbooks, handover, ongoing support.</div></div></li></ul></div><div class="w-tab-pane" data-w-tab="Tab 2"><ul aria-label="Protocols and products" class="process_steps" role="list"><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">1</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Roadmap</h3><p class="process_step-body">We map your integration surface to the target network and size the work.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> integration map and sizing.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">2</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Proposal</h3><p class="process_step-body">Milestone-based scope, with or without an ecosystem program behind it.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> milestone proposal, program application where one applies.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">3</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Build</h3><p class="process_step-body">Native contracts, adapters and SDKs, tested against your existing suite.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> contracts, adapters and SDKs passing your test suite.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">4</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Mainnet</h3><p class="process_step-body">Launch, docs, and a maintenance plan your engineers can run.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> mainnet launch, docs, maintenance plan.</div></div></li></ul></div><div class="w-tab-pane" data-w-tab="Tab 3"><ul aria-label="Ecosystems and foundations" class="process_steps" role="list"><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">1</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">DevX audit</h3><p class="process_step-body">Two engineers, two weeks, on your real onboarding path.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> audit report of the onboarding path, ranked friction points.</div></div></li><li class="process_step"><div class="process_step-num">2</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Roadmap</h3><p class="process_step-body">Tooling priorities with the ecosystem's engineering team.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> prioritized tooling roadmap.</div></div></li><li class="process_step" data-rv="eco-build"><div class="process_step-num">3</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Build</h3><p class="process_step-body">CLIs, scaffolding, sandboxes, registries, wallets.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> shipped tooling, open source, with docs.</div></div></li><li class="process_step" data-rv="eco-maintain"><div class="process_step-num">4</div><h3 class="process_step-h3">Maintain</h3><p class="process_step-body">Quarterly public-goods proposal and review.</p><div class="process_step-output"><div class="process_step-output-label">Output:</div><div class="inline-text"> maintained releases and a quarterly proposal.</div></div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></section>
